    <DataNode elementId="AT2G34770-MONOMER" textLabel="Dihydroceramide fatty acyl 2-hydroxylase FAH1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="O48916" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="300" centerY="395" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">Unlike the yeast homolog, the Arabidopsis protein does not contain a cytochrome b5 domain. The Arabidopsis protein, heterologously expressed in a yeast mutant lacking the alpha-hydroxylase activity, was able to functional complement the yeast mutant. It restored the content of alpha-hydroxy C26:0 fatty acid with the expanse of its C26:0 precursor.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT2G34770-MONOMER" />
