    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT1G14290-MONOMER" textLabel="AT1G14290-MONOMER" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9AST3" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="600" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL Arabidopsis has two isoenzymes of sphinganine 4-hydroxylase. The activities of the two isoenzymes were confirmed by heterologous expression in the yeast sur2 mutant lacking sphinganine 4-hydroxylase. HPLC, EI-MS and NMR analysis of the products accumulated in yeast transformants clearly showed that the isoenzyme encoded by AT1G14290 converts D-erythro-sphinganine into D-ribo-4-hydroxysphinganine in a stereospecific manner. Properties of the two isoenzymes are not further characterized.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G14290-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G14290.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9AST3" />
      <Property key="Catalyzes" value="RXN-33604, RXN-12498" />
      <Property key="CatalyzesCount" value="2" />
      <Property key="Accession1" value="AT1G14290.1" />
      <Property key="Gene" value="AT1G14290" />
      <Property key="InstanceNameTemplate" value="MONOMER-*" />
      <CitationRef elementRef="citation_PUB_11297741" />
    </DataNode>
    <DataNode elementId="AT3G61580-MONOMER" textLabel="Delta(8)-fatty-acid desaturase 1" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q9ZRP7" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="475" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">NIL The N-terminal sequence of the Arabidopsis protein is characteristic of cytochrome b5. Cytochrome b5 is the electron donor of many known desaturases. The fusion of cytochrom b5 with delta-8 sphingolipid desaturase may be a functional advantage. Heterologous expressing of the protein in yeast demonstrated that it is capable to convert the endogenous C18 phytosphinganine to phytosphingenine. Two regioisomeric phytosphingenines were formed with a 3:1 ratio of delta-8 and delta-9 double bonds. The enzyme is stereo-unselective and the desaturation products contain both cis- and trans-isomers. Note that the delta-9 regioisomers formed in the yeast transformants are not found in natural plant long chain bases. It was later indicated to be artifacts of analysis|CITS: [Lynch04]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G61580-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT3G61580.1" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Uniprot" value="Q9ZRP7" />
